\section{Data and universe}\label{sec:data}
<< V('univ.matches') >> resolved ATP/WTA/Challenger singles moneylines with \(\geq\)<< V('univ.minvol') >> volume,
<< V('univ.first') >> to << V('univ.last') >>: binary contracts on a public order book with free trade data. IS is the
first 80\% of matches by start time; OOS the last << V('univ.oos') >> from << V('univ.oosstart') >>
(<< V('univ.oos_vol') >> of volume; burned for v2). A blind test on << V('u2.markets') >> smaller markets checks the
volume filter's survivorship. << V('data.offsetcap') >> tapes may be truncated (kept); << V('data.nofee') >> early
matches without a fee schedule pay 0\%; << V('data.res5050') >> settle 50/50 (kept); tape stamps lag
<< V('data.blocklag') >>\,s. Sources: Polymarket APIs and sports websocket \citep{pmapi}; ESPN and WTA, latency only
