% ======================================================================================== 4 Methodology
\section{Methodology}\label{sec:method}
\para{Fast tier and v2} A detector fires on a \(\geq\)<< V('pol.det_c') >>¢ move of the 10\,s VWAP against the prior
60\,s. Each month a wallet qualifies on past months only (\(\geq\)<< V('pol.q_prints') >> prints 0--3\,s after a
detection, \(\geq\)<< V('pol.q_matches') >> matches, \(t > << V('pol.q_t') >>\) on its 30\,s markout). The frozen book
v2 copies qualifying prints, sized \(\propto 1/\sqrt{q(1-q)}\), at most << V('risk.order_usd') >> per order and
<< V('risk.netcap') >> shares net per match, held to resolution, at the fast tier's own prices: \emph{the opportunity at
their speed, not our execution}.

\para{CV strategy} Our tracker gets << V('cv.tt.tp50') >> of << V('cv.tt.called50') >> out-calls right 50\,ms before
contact on held-out 120\,fps table-tennis video (Fig.~\ref{fig:ladder}b) and streams << V('cv.eng.frames') >> frames at
<< V('cv.eng.fps') >>\,fps on one GPU with << V('cv.eng.dropped') >> drops. With the bounce at time zero, an order wins
only if
\begin{equation}\label{eq:budget}
  V + \delta + D - \ell \;<\; L + R \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad V \;<\; L + R - D - \delta + \ell ,
\end{equation}
where \(V\) is the feed delay, \(\delta\) the inference (<< V('cv.inf') >>\,ms), network and gateway delays, \(D\) the
<< V('venue.delay') >>\,s taker delay, \(\ell\) the CV call lead, \(L\) the stamp lag and \(R\) the reprice relative to
the stamp. \(R\), depth, network and fees are measured on << V('lat.n_points') >> live points; \(V\) and \(L\) are
assumed: \(V\) runs 0--60\,s (<< V('cv.seeds') >> seeds per cell) and the unmeasured \(L\) gets two readings,
pre-registered << V('cv.pre.lag') >>\,s and calibrated, post hoc << V('cv.cal.lag') >>\,s.

\para{Costs} Each match's own taker fee,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:fee}
  f(q) = r\,q\,(1-q)\ \text{per share} \;=\; 10{,}000\,r\,(1-q)\ \text{bps of notional},
\end{equation}
with \(r = << V('fee.rate') >>\) today (<< V('fee.bps_q05') >>\,bps at \(q = 0.5\)): << V('v2.is.fee_bps') >>\,/\,<< V('v2.oos.fee_bps') >>\,bps
on v2's trades (IS\,/\,OOS). Spreads are paid as traded. Stresses: ½ and 1 tick worse entry, fees \(\times\)2,
all costs \(\times\)2 (\(\approx\)+<< V('v2.is.hs_bps') >>\,bps more). \para{Validation} Monthly walk-forward inside IS;
past-month qualification; the fee in force; the onset look-ahead fixed (D9); every OOS read logged.

